Dashboard (brief §1): the summary band shows Projects and Live only; the
project cards keep name/id, questions, live/test/completed responses and
status and no longer show spend; the balance filter, the spend sorts and
the large wallet panel are gone. Usage tracking and billing are untouched —
the meters are still read and written exactly as before, they are simply
not drawn on the list.

Project Overview (§2): a project now opens on `/studio/<id>` as an overview
— information, configuration states, utilization in dollars, navigation to
every module, recent activity — and `?tab=` / `?mode=` / `?split=` deep
links keep opening the Studio directly, so every existing link, refresh and
bookmark still works. `GET /api/surveys/{id}/overview` reads the saved
definition, the deployments, the live quota counters, the reports, runs
and sample sources, the project configuration, the meter and the audit
log; `lib/projectOverview.ts` turns them into Configured / Incomplete /
Not set up / Needs attention per module from saved data only (no state is
inferred from the lifecycle status or hard-coded). `/sandbox/overview`
renders the same component for the browser suites.

Wallet (§3): `GET /api/billing/wallet`; `WalletMenu` is a compact
two-decimal pill in the top-right account area of the Dashboard, Analytics
and Studio headers, with the precise balance in its title and a menu for
Add funds (the page's own dialog where there is one, else /billing),
Usage & billing and Transaction history; it re-reads after a request. The
Studio's menubar gains `Project spend: $x.xx` beside Mode from the same
meter view the usage panel uses — the project's spend, distinct from the
wallet — and an "← Overview" link in the top bar.

Activity (§8): status changes and version restores are now audited as
`survey.status_changed` / `version.restored`, so they appear in Recent
activity with the other events; nothing is invented.

